{"name":"Michaelmas Daisy","hex":"#8881b0","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"daisy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wild flowering plant of species Bellis perennis of the family Asteraceae, with a yellow head and white petals","Any of numerous other flowering plants of various species, mostly among the asterids."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daisy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aster (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Aster is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Asteraceae. Its circumscription has been narrowed, and it now encompasses around 170 species, all but one of which are restricted to Eurasia; many species formerly in Aster are now in other genera of the tribe Astereae. Aster amellus is the type species of the genus and the family Asteraceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/330px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_(genus)","wikidata":"Q517130"},{"title":"Symphyotrichum","blocks":[{"text":"Symphyotrichum is a genus of over 100 species and naturally occurring hybrids of herbaceous annual and perennial plants in the composite family, Asteraceae, most which were formerly treated within the genus Aster. The majority are endemic to North America, but several also occur in the West Indies, Central and South America, as well as one species in eastern Eurasia. Several species have been introduced to Europe as garden specimens, most notably New England aster and New York aster."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Symphyotrichum_ericoides_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg/330px-Symphyotrichum_ericoides_-_Flickr_-_aspidoscelis_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symphyotrichum","wikidata":"Q2629596"},{"title":"Michaelmas","blocks":[{"text":"Michaelmas, also known as the Feast of Saints Michael, Gabriel and Raphael, the Feast of the Archangels, and the Feast of Saint Michael and All Angels, is a Christian festival observed in many Western Christian liturgical calendars on 29 September, and on 8 November in the Eastern Christian traditions. Michaelmas has been one of the four quarter days of the English and Irish financial, judicial and academic year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Linz_StMartin01.JPG/330px-Linz_StMartin01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michaelmas","wikidata":"Q3360565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/500px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/500px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAsteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/500px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/1280px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/500px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multi layer petals Aster flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAster_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Aster-alpinus.JPG/500px-Aster-alpinus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c